.TH opdict 1 "2026 November 14" ""

.SH NAME
opdict \- Opcode dictionary

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opdict
[processor] [mnemonic|opcode]

.SH COPYRIGHT
CoreLAB is Copyright (C) 2026 by Pozsar Zsolt.

.SH DESCRIPTION
The opdict script serves as an opcode dictionary for various processors.
It allows users to search for opcodes or mnemonics either interactively or via
a direct command-line query. In interactive mode, users can switch processor
types, list available processors, and query instructions.
.PP
The script is useable on Unix-like operating systems.

.SH BUILTIN COMMANDS
.TP
.B :q
Exit the interactive prompt.
.TP
.B :l
List available processor types.
.TP
.B :<cpu>
Change processor type to the specified <cpu> (e.g., :8080).

.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/share/corelab/cpu_*.csv.gz:
Processor opcode database files in compressed CSV format. (The path may vary.)

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B 1
Insufficient parameters.
.TP
.B 2
Missing dependency.

